{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdP2VKkmtPsshSJ5Kazci","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Z6DU2BWzm5LHTfMJde5Di","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.53CZOI/SOLUTION.md","content":"# Solution\n\nTwo bugs in `lrucache/cache.py` broke the LRU semantics:\n\n1. **`get` didn't refresh recency.** A successful `get` returned the value but\n   never moved the key to the most-recently-used end of the `OrderedDict`. So an\n   accessed key was still treated as least-recently-used and got evicted on the\n   next `put`. Fixed by calling `self._data.move_to_end(key)` before returning.\n\n2. **`put` evicted before checking for an existing key.** The eviction check was\n   `if len(self._data) >= self.capacity`, which fired even when the key already\n   existed (an in-place update). At full capacity, updating a key wrongly popped\n   the least-recently-used entry. Fixed by only evicting for genuinely new keys:\n   `if key not in self._data and len(self._data) >= self.capacity`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":188,"cache_read_input_tokens":24874,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":188,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8aa9f946-e546-4ea0-a3bf-68e26b43aa53","uuid":"8bc6ab16-0fc2-448a-91ff-e2608b27eccd","timestamp":"2026-07-25T15:39:09.989Z","request_id":"req_011CdP2VJ3b96m2LiiFd882F"}
